# Crockpot API — /recipes
#
# GET /recipes, GET /recipes/:id — CROC-015. Both behind OptionalAuthMiddleware
# (no token → anonymous; bad/expired token → anonymous, never 401). Run this
# file top-to-bottom: the POST section below seeds an ADMIN (approved) recipe
# as {{recipeId}}, then the GET section reads it back. Non-admin / own-unapproved
# visibility is covered at the handler + repository layers with mocked claims
# and a real dev DB (internal/handler/recipe_handler_test.go,
# internal/repository/recipe_list_test.go) — this file uses the ADMIN account
# so an admin sees every recipe regardless.
#
# POST /recipes — CROC-014. Any authenticated user (no role gate); the
# only role-dependent behaviour is `approved` (true for ADMIN, false
# otherwise) and the FREE-tier 5-recipe cap. This file runs with the
# ADMIN test account (same one-time bump as item-categories.http /
# units.http — see requests/README.md), so every happy-path create here
# comes back `approved: true`, and the 409 recipe_limit_reached / non-
# admin `approved: false` paths are NOT reachable from this file — those
# are covered at the handler layer with mocked claims
# (internal/handler/recipe_handler_test.go).
#
# Focus: the wiring — a create that persists recipe + ingredients +
# categories, and the 400 validation / invalid-reference translations.
#
# GET /recipes/time-range — CROC-043. Public, no auth. {minTime, maxTime}
# over approved recipes only, live query, no server-side cache.
#
# POST/DELETE /recipes/:id/favourite, GET /recipes/favourites — CROC-018.
# All three behind full AuthMiddleware (no anonymous path, unlike GET
# /recipes). The favourite section below runs the whole
# favourite → appears in list + isFavourite true → unfavourite →
# disappears from list + isFavourite false loop against the seeded
# {{recipeId}} using the ADMIN token, then a separate auth/validation
# section for the 401/400/404 cases.
#
# Fixtures below create two throwaway `items` rows (the catalog is empty
# until CROC-024): one unconstrained, one constrained to a single unit,
# so both the invalid_unit_id and unit_not_allowed_for_item paths can be
# exercised. Cleanup is a SQL note at the bottom — there is no
# DELETE /recipes endpoint until CROC-016.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Fixtures — real reference data + two throwaway items
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Real item category to hang the throwaway items off.
# @name itemCategory
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/item-categories

###

@itemCategoryId = {{itemCategory.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Real seeded units.
# @name units
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/units

###

@unitId1 = {{units.response.body.$[0].id}}
@unitId2 = {{units.response.body.$[1].id}}

### Real seeded recipe categories.
# @name recipeCategories
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories

###

@recipeCategoryId1 = {{recipeCategories.response.body.$[0].id}}
@recipeCategoryId2 = {{recipeCategories.response.body.$[1].id}}

### Throwaway item — unconstrained (no allowed units).
# @name itemFree
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-recipe-item",
  "categoryId": "{{itemCategoryId}}"
}

###

@itemId = {{itemFree.response.body.id}}

### Throwaway item — constrained to unitId1 only.
# @name itemConstrained
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-recipe-item-constrained",
  "categoryId": "{{itemCategoryId}}",
  "allowedUnitIds": ["{{unitId1}}"]
}

###

@itemIdConstrained = {{itemConstrained.response.body.id}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /recipes — happy path
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 201 — full recipe (ADMIN account → approved: true), one ingredient
### with a unit + one without, two categories, an image.
# @name create
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test Slow Cooker Beef Stew",
  "timeInMinutes": 360,
  "serves": 4,
  "instructions": ["Brown the beef", "Add everything else", "Cook low for 6 hours"],
  "notes": ["Freezes well", ""],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId1}}", "{{recipeCategoryId2}}"],
  "ingredients": [
    { "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "unitId": "{{unitId1}}", "quantity": 800 },
    { "itemId": "{{itemIdConstrained}}", "unitId": "{{unitId1}}", "quantity": 2 }
  ],
  "image": {
    "url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/v1/beef-stew.jpg",
    "filename": "beef-stew"
  }
}

###

@recipeId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### ✅ 201 — minimal recipe (no notes, no image, one unitless ingredient).
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test Minimal Recipe",
  "timeInMinutes": 20,
  "serves": 2,
  "instructions": ["Just cook it"],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId1}}"],
  "ingredients": [
    { "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": 3 }
  ]
}

###


